# Hey Jude, bridge (figure 14.2)
# Eleven and a half bars. Pollack's "-7" bars are the F chord turned into F7 (V-of-IV). The
# bassline is typed only for the first phrase; the blank under bar 5 is read as the F held.
# In the second phrase the F7 bar is shortened by half: it is drawn as two beats of a full bar.
#? Bass octave chosen for range (Bb2 down to C2, up to F2).
#? The half bar (F7 for two beats) will play with a two-beat gap after it.
